[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2712688183","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103954#issuecomment-2712688183","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103954","id":2712688183,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hsFY3","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T05:26:22Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T05:37:35Z","body":"Looks like the problem was introduced in 4.4 dev1\n\nEdit: Traced it back to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/95640. In 4.3 we didn't include draw calls from transparent objects in the monitor. That bug was fixed by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/95640\n\nLooking at performance, on my M2 MBP, Performance is 5%-10% faster in 4.4 than it was in 4.3 with this test scene. \n\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2712688183/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2714645614","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103954#issuecomment-2714645614","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103954","id":2714645614,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hzjRu","user":{"login":"bikemurt","id":23486102,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNDg2MTAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23486102?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt","html_url":"https://github.com/bikemurt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T14:55:05Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T16:46:07Z","body":"Interesting- so what I thought was a performance loss was just a bug with the counters, which has been fixed. I confirmed the actual rendering behaviour is the same in RenderDoc between 4.3-stable and 4.4-stable (roughly the same number of calls to `vkCmdDrawIndexed`).\n\nIs an optimization even possible here? Maybe there is something about depth pre-pass that I don't understand. To my knowledge there's a pre-pass where alpha values below 0.99 are discarded, this is rendered as opaque for the depth buffer (and shadows?). Then the transparency is rendered back-to-front after as a part of the main render. Is there some fundamental conflict between sorting for depth pre-pass and sorting for the main render pass? My assumption has been that the front-to-back sorting for opaque materials was always handled separately from the back-to-front sorting for transparent draw calls.\n\nEdit: depth layer is in the sort key, and presumably during depth pre-pass (alpha) is where transparent meshes get stacked back-to-front: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a77a28c02951def7a7e2c3457259a60260a40abe/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_clustered/render_forward_clustered.h#L487-L499\n\nWhen checking for batching, we check for identical keys between calls (after sorting): https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a77a28c02951def7a7e2c3457259a60260a40abe/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_clustered/render_forward_clustered.cpp#L834\n\nMakes me wonder though - is being on a different depth layer an actual render state change? It would be interesting to mask out the depth layer information when checking to see if two keys are equal. I may give this a try.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2714645614/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715235946","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103954#issuecomment-2715235946","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103954","id":2715235946,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6h1zZq","user":{"login":"bikemurt","id":23486102,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNDg2MTAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23486102?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt","html_url":"https://github.com/bikemurt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T17:59:06Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T18:15:04Z","body":"A little more investigation shows that we are losing the sortation on `material_id` in the transparent color pass. Haven't figured out why yet.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d3b69e6a-918c-43d0-9583-ac3928e6101c\n\nEdit: probably this https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a77a28c02951def7a7e2c3457259a60260a40abe/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_clustered/render_forward_clustered.cpp#L1855.\n\nI'm realizing there's a conflict between trying to sort by material and trying to sort by reverse depth. Open to suggestions on this. I'd love to hear if there's any possible way to squeeze some more optimization in here (my game could certainly benefit from it).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715235946/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715328376","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103954#issuecomment-2715328376","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103954","id":2715328376,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6h2J94","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T18:25:53Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T18:25:53Z","body":"Doing a quick test. It looks like transparents do batch, but sorting by depth takes priority. This is important because transparent objects need to be sorted by depth otherwise they will be totally broken. Importantly, we can't sort based on material ID because that will very often result in things being drawn in the wrong order. \n\nThe problem with your test scene is that it changes the material so frequently that it breaks batching. Take a look at a simpler test scene with only two materials and a single line split between them.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dc054469-4066-46ae-9e3c-52e77c7166cb)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715328376/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715612496","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103954#issuecomment-2715612496","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103954","id":2715612496,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6h3PVQ","user":{"login":"bikemurt","id":23486102,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNDg2MTAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23486102?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt","html_url":"https://github.com/bikemurt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T20:18:28Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T20:18:28Z","body":"> Importantly, we can't sort based on material ID because that will very often result in things being drawn in the wrong order.\n\nOk. I'm happy to close the issue if you believe no further optimization can be had here.\n\nOne more thought - in theory, if you organized a set of multimeshes, one for each material type, then you would get 3 draw calls. Assuming depth pre-pass transparency is still on for those three multimeshes, then what would be different in this situation vs. batching if you sort by material first, then depth (ignoring `priority` for a moment)?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715612496/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715622887","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103954#issuecomment-2715622887","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103954","id":2715622887,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6h3R3n","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T20:23:41Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T20:23:41Z","body":"Both would break depending on what angle you are viewing from. One material will draw over all the others regardless of the relative position of the objects. \n\nWith depth pre-pass transparency it will appear to work if your meshes are fully opaque as they are in the MRP. But if your objects are fully opaque, you should not be using the transparent pipeline. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715622887/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715629349","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103954#issuecomment-2715629349","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103954","id":2715629349,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6h3Tcl","user":{"login":"bikemurt","id":23486102,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNDg2MTAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23486102?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt","html_url":"https://github.com/bikemurt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T20:27:01Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T20:27:01Z","body":"Gotcha. In my case it's background billboards with transparent textures, so I do need the transparent pipeline. Covering the background with larger imposter billboards really didn't look at that good in my case, so I went for 1 tree = 1 billboard. At my lowest level (LOD0) these are organized into multimesh instances, one per tree type (9 in total), and it really doesn't appear to have any visual artifacts, but I hear what you are saying. On some level, the multimesh ordering will not match what the correct alpha order would be if they were all instances.\n\nI'll leave it open for a bit more in case anyone else has anythoughts.\n\nThe good news is that 4.4 is accurately reporting draw calls now, so I know what I'm optimizing!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715629349/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2719410374","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103954#issuecomment-2719410374","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103954","id":2719410374,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iFujG","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T00:18:14Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T00:18:14Z","body":"Reopening, as this should be documented in the manual where relevant.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2719410374/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]